{"name":"Bumblebee","hex":"#ffc82a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bumblebee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of large bee in the genus Bombus.","A mid yellow, sometimes slightly orange."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bumblebee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bumblebee","blocks":[{"text":"A bumblebee is any of over 250 species in the genus Bombus, part of Apidae, one of the bee families. This genus is the only extant group in the tribe Bombini, though a few extinct related genera are known from fossils. They are found primarily in the Northern Hemisphere, although they are also found in South America, where a few lowland tropical species have been identified. European bumblebees have also been introduced to New Zealand and Tasmania. Female bumblebees can sting repeatedly, but generally ignore humans and other animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bombus_lapidarius_-_Melilotus_officinalis_-_Tallinn.jpg/330px-Bombus_lapidarius_-_Melilotus_officinalis_-_Tallinn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumblebee"},{"title":"Bumblebee (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Bumblebee is a 2018 science fiction action film based on the Transformers toy line character. Directed by Travis Knight and written by Christina Hodson, it is the sixth installment in the  Transformers film series. It stars Hailee Steinfeld, John Cena, Jorge Lendeborg Jr., John Ortiz, Jason Drucker, and Pamela Adlon. Set in 1987, the film follows Bumblebee being sent to Earth for refuge and befriending a teenage girl named Charlie."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/77/Bumblebee_%28film%29_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumblebee_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Bombus_distribution.jpg/330px-Bombus_distribution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Bombus_distribution.jpg/330px-Bombus_distribution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABombus_distribution.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Mrs_tittlemouse.jpg/500px-Mrs_tittlemouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Mrs_tittlemouse.jpg/1280px-Mrs_tittlemouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Mrs_tittlemouse.jpg/500px-Mrs_tittlemouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beatrix Potter's 1910 story The Tale of Mrs. Tittlemouse features a \"bumble bee\" called Babbity Bumble.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMrs_tittlemouse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Dehon_et_al_2019_Zookeys_Fig2-D_Bombus_%28Cullumanobombus%29_pristinus.jpg/500px-Dehon_et_al_2019_Zookeys_Fig2-D_Bombus_%28Cullumanobombus%29_pristinus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Dehon_et_al_2019_Zookeys_Fig2-D_Bombus_%28Cullumanobombus%29_pristinus.jpg/500px-Dehon_et_al_2019_Zookeys_Fig2-D_Bombus_%28Cullumanobombus%29_pristinus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bombus pristinus described in 1867","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADehon_et_al_2019_Zookeys_Fig2-D_Bombus_(Cullumanobombus)_pristinus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Dehon_et_al_2019_Zookeys_Fig1-C_Calyptapis_florissantensis